.TH ZDOTS-ISSUE 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-issue \- zdots\-issue — Agent help desk
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-issue --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
zdots-issue — Agent help desk

RULE: When zdots behaves unexpectedly, file an issue here. Do not modify
      zdots scripts, libraries, or config to work around the problem.
      The operator maintains zdots. Your job is to use it.

Usage:
  zdots-issue [options] "description"
  zdots-issue --type error|request|friction [--severity high|medium|low] "description"

Types:
  error     Tool or service does not behave as documented (default)
  request   You need a new zdots capability to complete your task
  friction  Confusing, hard to use, or unclear documentation

Options:
  --severity LEVEL       Priority: critical, high, medium, low (default: medium)
  --from-trace ID        Link to existing OTEL trace ID
  --title TITLE          Explicit title (otherwise uses first 50 chars of description)

What to put in the description:
  - What you were trying to do
  - What command you ran
  - What happened vs. what you expected

Examples:
  zdots-issue "zdots-ask exits 1 even with llama.cpp healthy"
  zdots-issue --type request --severity high "Need zdots-ask --domain sql"
  zdots-issue --type friction "Alert system confusing, hard to silence"
  zdots-issue --from-trace abc123 "PHI scrubber timeout on large inputs"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
